{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLrw4hLochYtqiMeuvqn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`Line.is_parallel` and the other three methods now raise `TypeError` for invalid input instead of `AttributeError`. The existing tests in `sympy/geometry/tests/test_line.py` pass (36 passed). I didn't run the issue's `Line.is_parallel(Line(Point(0,0), Point(1,1)), Point(0,0))` example directly, and I didn't add a test for the new behavior.\n\nThe type check in `sympy/geometry/line.py` used `and` where it needed `or`. It only raised when both arguments were not `LinearEntity`, so a single bad argument got through to `.direction` and crashed. I changed `and` to `or` in the four places the check appears, which cover `is_parallel`, `is_perpendicular`, `angle_between` and `smallest_angle_between`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":290,"cache_read_input_tokens":19467,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":290},"output_tokens":267,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a9eb00be-de67-4ec6-a886-dc75d096aaf2","uuid":"9bcffa65-6c52-4174-9e77-3dfa48469b03","timestamp":"2026-11-24T01:10:28.066Z","request_id":"req_011ChLrw4YAZPfMi4z2wFcYw"}
